# Attribution and source boundaries

This project references public catalogue metadata and URLs from the eight
repository owners listed in `catalog/upstreams.json`. Each upstream owns its
own code, packages, release process, artwork and trademarks.

Public visibility is not a redistribution license. As of this project's
initial review, only `kas021/Testing-Modules-AR` exposed a root `LICENSE`
(MIT); this workflow does not repackage its code either. Do not infer a license
for any other upstream repository without checking its current terms.

The merge intentionally **does not** copy source code, signed connector files,
ZIP packages or artwork from external repositories into `Haimiya612/Kinetiq-Modules`.
It stores names, version descriptors, upstream links, hash strings and format
capability flags to support discovery and compatibility work. All installable
binaries remain hosted by their original publisher.

